{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KguycHVjKrhtfKYarHmA1j","type":"tool_result","content":"340\t\\label{sec:conclusion}\n341\t%==============================================================================\n342\t\n343\tWe introduced the temporal label model, a time-aware extension of data programming that models LF temporal dynamics (leading/concurrent/lagging roles) via an HMM. On a human-annotated gold set ($\\kappa{=}0.82$), \\tlm{} improves label quality by 12.2~pp over majority vote and 5.9~pp over FlyingSquid. \\ours{}, a lightweight GRU probe trained on \\tlm{} labels, achieves 0.86 macro-F1---surpassing the LF oracle by 6.0~pp (``student exceeds teacher'') and LLM-as-judge (CoT) by 4.5~pp at $690\\times$ lower latency. Cross-agent evaluation demonstrates that the probe captures generalizable progress signals ($-6.7$~pp transfer degradation vs.\\ $-21.6$~pp for the LF oracle). A simulated early-termination policy based on probe predictions saves 27\\% of tokens while preserving 97\\% of successful outcomes.\n344\t\n345\t%==============================================================================\n346\t% References\n347\t%==============================================================================\n348\t%\\bibliography{references}\n349\t\n350\t% Inline bibliography for self-contained compilation\n351\t\\begin{thebibliography}{20}\n352\t\n353\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Ratner et al.}2017]{ratner2017snorkel}\n354\tAlexander Ratner, Stephen Bach, Henry Ehrenberg, Jason Fries, Sen Wu, and Christopher R\\'{e}. 2017.\n355\t\\newblock Snorkel: Rapid Training Data Creation with Weak Supervision.\n356\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ VLDB}, 11(3):269--282.\n357\t\n358\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Fu et al.}2020]{fu2020fast}\n359\tDaniel Fu, Mayee Chen, Frederic Sala, Sarah Hooper, Kayvon Fatahalian, and Christopher R\\'{e}. 2020.\n360\t\\newblock Fast and Three-rious: Speeding Up Weak Supervision with Triplet Methods.\n361\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ ICML}.\n362\t\n363\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Lightman et al.}2023]{lightman2023lets}\n364\tHunter Lightman, Vineet Kosaraju, Yura Burda, Harri Edwards, Bowen Baker, Teddy Lee, Jan Leike, John Schulman, Ilya Sutskever, and Karl Cobbe. 2023.\n365\t\\newblock Let's Verify Step by Step.\n366\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2305.20050}.\n367\t\n368\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et al.}2024a]{wang2024mathshepherd}\n369\tPeiyi Wang, Lei Li, Zhihong Shao, R.X.\\ Xu, Damai Dai, Yifei Li, Deli Chen, Y.\\ Wu, and Zhifang Sui. 2024.\n370\t\\newblock Math-Shepherd: Verify and Reinforce LLMs Step-by-step without Human Annotations.\n371\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ ACL}.\n372\t\n373\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Yang et al.}2024]{yang2024sweagent}\n374\tJohn Yang, Carlos Jimenez, Alexander Wettig, Kilian Lieret, Shunyu Yao, Karthik Narasimhan, and Ofir Press. 2024.\n375\t\\newblock SWE-agent: Agent-Computer Interfaces Enable Automated Software Engineering.\n376\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2405.15793}.\n377\t\n378\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et al.}2024b]{wang2024opendevin}\n379\tXingyao Wang, Boxuan Li, Yufan Song, Frank Xu, Xiangru Tang, Mingchen Zhuge, Jiayi Pan, Yueqi Song, Bowen Li, et al. 2024.\n380\t\\newblock OpenDevin: An Open Platform for AI Software Developers as Generalist Agents.\n381\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2407.16741}.\n382\t\n383\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Yao et al.}2023]{yao2023react}\n384\tShunyu Yao, Jeffrey Zhao, Dian Yu, Nan Du, Izhak Shafran, Karthik Narasimhan, and Yuan Cao. 2023.\n385\t\\newblock ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models.\n386\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ ICLR}.\n387\t\n388\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Shinn et al.}2023]{shinn2023reflexion}\n389\tNoah Shinn, Federico Cassano, Ashwin Gopinath, Karthik Narasimhan, and Shunyu Yao. 2023.\n390\t\\newblock Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning.\n391\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n392\t\n393\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Yao et al.}2024]{yao2024tree}\n394\tShunyu Yao, Dian Yu, Jeffrey Zhao, Izhak Shafran, Tom Griffiths, Yuan Cao, and Karthik Narasimhan. 2024.\n395\t\\newblock Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models.\n396\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n397\t\n398\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Hao et al.}2023]{hao2023reasoning}\n399\tShibo Hao, Yi Gu, Haodi Ma, Joshua Hong, Zhen Wang, Daisy Wang, and Zhiting Hu. 2023.\n400\t\\newblock Reasoning with Language Model is Planning with World Model.\n401\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ EMNLP}.\n402\t\n403\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zheng et al.}2024]{zheng2024judging}\n404\tLianmin Zheng, Wei-Lin Chiang, Ying Sheng, Siyuan Zhuang, Zhanghao Wu, Yonghao Zhuang, Zi Lin, Zhuohan Li, Dacheng Li, et al. 2024.\n405\t\\newblock Judging LLM-as-a-Judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena.\n406\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n407\t\n408\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{DuBois et al.}2024]{dubois2024alpacafarm}\n409\tYann DuBois, Chen Xuechen Li, Rohan Taori, Tianyi Zhang, Ishaan Gulrajani, Jimmy Ba, Carlos Guestrin, Percy Liang, and Tatsunori Hashimoto. 2024.\n410\t\\newblock AlpacaFarm: A Simulation Framework for Methods that Learn from Human Feedback.\n411\t\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n412\t\n413\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Uesato et al.}2022]{uesato2022solving}\n414\tJonathan Uesato, Nate Kushman, Ramana Kumar, Francis Song, Noah Siegel, Lisa Wang, Antonia Creswell, Geoffrey Irving, and Irina Higgins. 2022.\n415\t\\newblock Solving Math Word Problems with Process- and Outcome-Based Feedback.\n416\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2211.14275}.\n417\t\n418\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zhuge et al.}2024]{zhuge2024cdcs}\n419\tMingchen Zhuge, Changsheng Zhao, Dylan Ashley, Wenyi Wang, Dmitrii Khizbullin, and J\\\"{u}rgen Schmidhuber. 2024.\n420\t\\newblock Agent Workflow Memory.\n421\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2409.07429}.\n422\t\n423\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zhang et al.}2024]{zhang2024specra}\n424\tYufan Zhang, Hongzhan Lin, and Tao Xie. 2024.\n425\t\\newblock SpecRA: Speculation-based Runtime Analysis for LLM Agent Loops.\n426\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}.\n427\t\n428\t\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Li et al.}2024]{li2024trajad}\n429\tYuxin Li, et al. 2024.\n430\t\\newblock TrajAD: Trajectory Anomaly Detection in LLM Agents.\n431\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}.\n432\t\n433\t\\end{thebibliography}\n434\t\n435\t%==============================================================================\n436\t\\appendix\n437\t\\section{Supplementary Results}\n438\t%==============================================================================\n439\t\n440\t\\subsection{Full Architecture Ablation}\n441\t\\label{app:arch}\n442\t\n443\tTable~\\ref{tab:arch-full} presents the full architecture comparison.\n444\t\n445\t\\begin{table}[h]\n446\t\\centering\n447\t\\small\n448\t\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n449\t\\toprule"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c62cb88a-9d2d-484c-a1fc-f28f765eb6cd","uuid":"3ae378e6-5bac-43af-bd19-bf68105a0345","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:27:00.658Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T095527/best/paper.tex","content":"\\label{sec:conclusion}\n%==============================================================================\n\nWe introduced the temporal label model, a time-aware extension of data programming that models LF temporal dynamics (leading/concurrent/lagging roles) via an HMM. On a human-annotated gold set ($\\kappa{=}0.82$), \\tlm{} improves label quality by 12.2~pp over majority vote and 5.9~pp over FlyingSquid. \\ours{}, a lightweight GRU probe trained on \\tlm{} labels, achieves 0.86 macro-F1---surpassing the LF oracle by 6.0~pp (``student exceeds teacher'') and LLM-as-judge (CoT) by 4.5~pp at $690\\times$ lower latency. Cross-agent evaluation demonstrates that the probe captures generalizable progress signals ($-6.7$~pp transfer degradation vs.\\ $-21.6$~pp for the LF oracle). A simulated early-termination policy based on probe predictions saves 27\\% of tokens while preserving 97\\% of successful outcomes.\n\n%==============================================================================\n% References\n%==============================================================================\n%\\bibliography{references}\n\n% Inline bibliography for self-contained compilation\n\\begin{thebibliography}{20}\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Ratner et al.}2017]{ratner2017snorkel}\nAlexander Ratner, Stephen Bach, Henry Ehrenberg, Jason Fries, Sen Wu, and Christopher R\\'{e}. 2017.\n\\newblock Snorkel: Rapid Training Data Creation with Weak Supervision.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ VLDB}, 11(3):269--282.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Fu et al.}2020]{fu2020fast}\nDaniel Fu, Mayee Chen, Frederic Sala, Sarah Hooper, Kayvon Fatahalian, and Christopher R\\'{e}. 2020.\n\\newblock Fast and Three-rious: Speeding Up Weak Supervision with Triplet Methods.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ ICML}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Lightman et al.}2023]{lightman2023lets}\nHunter Lightman, Vineet Kosaraju, Yura Burda, Harri Edwards, Bowen Baker, Teddy Lee, Jan Leike, John Schulman, Ilya Sutskever, and Karl Cobbe. 2023.\n\\newblock Let's Verify Step by Step.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2305.20050}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et al.}2024a]{wang2024mathshepherd}\nPeiyi Wang, Lei Li, Zhihong Shao, R.X.\\ Xu, Damai Dai, Yifei Li, Deli Chen, Y.\\ Wu, and Zhifang Sui. 2024.\n\\newblock Math-Shepherd: Verify and Reinforce LLMs Step-by-step without Human Annotations.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ ACL}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Yang et al.}2024]{yang2024sweagent}\nJohn Yang, Carlos Jimenez, Alexander Wettig, Kilian Lieret, Shunyu Yao, Karthik Narasimhan, and Ofir Press. 2024.\n\\newblock SWE-agent: Agent-Computer Interfaces Enable Automated Software Engineering.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2405.15793}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Wang et al.}2024b]{wang2024opendevin}\nXingyao Wang, Boxuan Li, Yufan Song, Frank Xu, Xiangru Tang, Mingchen Zhuge, Jiayi Pan, Yueqi Song, Bowen Li, et al. 2024.\n\\newblock OpenDevin: An Open Platform for AI Software Developers as Generalist Agents.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2407.16741}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Yao et al.}2023]{yao2023react}\nShunyu Yao, Jeffrey Zhao, Dian Yu, Nan Du, Izhak Shafran, Karthik Narasimhan, and Yuan Cao. 2023.\n\\newblock ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ ICLR}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Shinn et al.}2023]{shinn2023reflexion}\nNoah Shinn, Federico Cassano, Ashwin Gopinath, Karthik Narasimhan, and Shunyu Yao. 2023.\n\\newblock Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Yao et al.}2024]{yao2024tree}\nShunyu Yao, Dian Yu, Jeffrey Zhao, Izhak Shafran, Tom Griffiths, Yuan Cao, and Karthik Narasimhan. 2024.\n\\newblock Tree of Thoughts: Deliberate Problem Solving with Large Language Models.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Hao et al.}2023]{hao2023reasoning}\nShibo Hao, Yi Gu, Haodi Ma, Joshua Hong, Zhen Wang, Daisy Wang, and Zhiting Hu. 2023.\n\\newblock Reasoning with Language Model is Planning with World Model.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ EMNLP}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zheng et al.}2024]{zheng2024judging}\nLianmin Zheng, Wei-Lin Chiang, Ying Sheng, Siyuan Zhuang, Zhanghao Wu, Yonghao Zhuang, Zi Lin, Zhuohan Li, Dacheng Li, et al. 2024.\n\\newblock Judging LLM-as-a-Judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{DuBois et al.}2024]{dubois2024alpacafarm}\nYann DuBois, Chen Xuechen Li, Rohan Taori, Tianyi Zhang, Ishaan Gulrajani, Jimmy Ba, Carlos Guestrin, Percy Liang, and Tatsunori Hashimoto. 2024.\n\\newblock AlpacaFarm: A Simulation Framework for Methods that Learn from Human Feedback.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Proc.\\ NeurIPS}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Uesato et al.}2022]{uesato2022solving}\nJonathan Uesato, Nate Kushman, Ramana Kumar, Francis Song, Noah Siegel, Lisa Wang, Antonia Creswell, Geoffrey Irving, and Irina Higgins. 2022.\n\\newblock Solving Math Word Problems with Process- and Outcome-Based Feedback.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2211.14275}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zhuge et al.}2024]{zhuge2024cdcs}\nMingchen Zhuge, Changsheng Zhao, Dylan Ashley, Wenyi Wang, Dmitrii Khizbullin, and J\\\"{u}rgen Schmidhuber. 2024.\n\\newblock Agent Workflow Memory.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2409.07429}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Zhang et al.}2024]{zhang2024specra}\nYufan Zhang, Hongzhan Lin, and Tao Xie. 2024.\n\\newblock SpecRA: Speculation-based Runtime Analysis for LLM Agent Loops.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}.\n\n\\bibitem[\\protect\\citename{Li et al.}2024]{li2024trajad}\nYuxin Li, et al. 2024.\n\\newblock TrajAD: Trajectory Anomaly Detection in LLM Agents.\n\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}.\n\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n%==============================================================================\n\\appendix\n\\section{Supplementary Results}\n%==============================================================================\n\n\\subsection{Full Architecture Ablation}\n\\label{app:arch}\n\nTable~\\ref{tab:arch-full} presents the full architecture comparison.\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\n\\small\n\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\n\\toprule","numLines":110,"startLine":340,"totalLines":559}}}
